The research's d81b32d (virtio-gpu-desktop, src/wl-cross-domain-proxy,
2026-10-22), on top of its work at 18cb8b2 (the file it changes is the same
at both): --drop-dcc-modifiers also leaves Intel CCS modifiers out of the
forwarded feedback.

On the Arc Pro B50 the nested KWin's output buffers carried a CCS modifier,
which Battlemage's display takes only from 64 KiB-aligned buffers
(xe_display_bo.c: intel_fb_needs_64k_phys); the guest's buffers made by the
host's Xe native context lack that, so every ADDFB2 failed and the host
composited every frame of the full-screen VM.  The same mechanism as AMD DCC
(the nested KWin allocates from the default tranche).

Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later, as the research's other changes to the proxy.

